-3.1 On $S^3\setminus K$, define $H_t$ to be the identity outside $N(K)$ and, in the punctured disk fibres with $0<|z|\le\epsilon$, set $H_t(\Phi(s,z))=\Phi(s,((1-t)|z|+t\epsilon)z/|z|)$ for $0\le t\le1$. The formula is continuous for $z\ne0$ and is the identity at $|z|=\epsilon$, so it glues continuously to the identity outside $N(K)$. It fixes every point of $E_K$, stays in $S^3\setminus K$, and at $t=1$ sends every point of the punctured tube to $T_K\subset E_K$. Hence $H_t$ is a strong deformation retraction of $S^3\setminus K$ onto $E_K$. [F2, step 1.1, step 2.1, construct, algebra] ∎
